<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bobolice</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bublitz</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bobolice, in German Bublitz, is a small town in West Pomeranian Voivodeship, north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. From the 13th century it belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamien-pomorski">Cammin</a> as part of their secular territory with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koszalin">Köslin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kolobrzeg">Kolberg</a>, passing with it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> after the Peace of Westphalia and to Poland in 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bobolice.jpg" alt="Bobolice" width="320" height="354" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Krygor · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ko%C5%9Bci%C3%B3%C5%82_par._p.w.Wniebowzi%C4%99cia_NMP_w_Bobolicach.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
